.Sh DESCRIPTION
Parses and builds .torrent metainfo files.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_metainfo_parse
loads from a bencoded buffer.
.Fn mbt_metainfo_new
allocates an empty object for programmatic construction.
.Fn mbt_metainfo_free
releases all resources, including embedded pieces and strings.
.Pp
The builder functions are:
.Fn mbt_metainfo_set_content
which reads files and computes SHA-1 piece hashes,
.Fn mbt_metainfo_add_tracker
for announce URLs,
.Fn mbt_metainfo_add_node
for DHT bootstrap entries,
.Fn mbt_metainfo_set_comment
and
.Fn mbt_metainfo_set_private
for optional top-level fields.
.Pp
All accessors return borrowed data valid only until
.Fa mi
is freed or rebuilt.
Accessors taking an
.Fa idx
are 0-based over the respective item list.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_metainfo_raw_info
returns the encoded info dict bytes, used for infohash computation
and BEP 9 info exchange serving.
.Fn mbt_metainfo_encode
serializes the full .torrent structure into a caller-allocated buffer
which must be freed by the caller after use.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Functions returning
.Ft int
return 0 on success or a negative errno value on failure.
Functions returning pointers return NULL on error.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Parse and print a torrent:
.Bd -literal
struct mbt_metainfo *mi;
unsigned char buf[128 * 1024];
size_t fsize = /* ... read file into buf ... */;

mbt_metainfo_parse(&mi, buf, fsize);
printf("name    : %s\n", mbt_metainfo_name(mi));
for (int i = 0; i < mbt_metainfo_file_count(mi); i++)
    printf("%2d: %s (%zu)\n", i,
        mbt_metainfo_file_path(mi, i),
        mbt_metainfo_file_length(mi, i));

unsigned char *encoded;
size_t elen;
mbt_metainfo_encode(mi, &encoded, &elen);
free(encoded);
mbt_metainfo_free(mi);
.Ed
